$ \sqrt[3]{6} \times \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{162}} = \sqrt[3]{6 \times \frac{1}{162}} $

Calculating the product inside:

$ 6 \times \frac{1}{162} = \frac{6}{162} = \frac{1}{27} $

Therefore,

$ \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{27}} $

Then, $ \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{27}} = \frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{27}} = \frac{1}{3} $

Therefore,

$ P = \left( \frac{1}{3} \right)^{-1} = 3 $


