Similarly, $ g(x + 3) \leq g(x + 2) \leq g(x) $, so $ g(x + 3) \leq g(x) $

Similarly, $ g(x + 4) \leq g(x + 3) \leq g(x) $, so $ g(x + 4) \leq g(x) $

Then, $ g(x + 5) \geq g(x) $

Therefore, combining these results:

$ g(x + 5) \geq g(x) $

and

$ g(x + 5) \leq g(x) $

